*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
server/linux/* text eol=lf
scripts/hooks/* text eol=lf
tools_py/release/leak_allow.txt text eol=lf
server/ops/*.sh text eol=lf
server/ops/backup.cron text eol=lf
server/ops/ops.env.example text eol=lf
# The npm workspace's parts (under web/ until 2026-10-02, RS.R4) and its root files: text, LF
socomlegacy/** text eol=lf
# The movie decoder and its source tarball are binaries, committed as they are (OT.R66, 2026-10-19): never normalized
socomlegacy/packages/fmv/wasm/out/* binary
landing/** text eol=lf
shared/** text eol=lf
package.json text eol=lf
package-lock.json text eol=lf
# The rules above normalise every path under the workspace's parts to text/LF, which corrupts binary font files
# (autocrlf strips bytes it mistakes for CRLF). Mark the vendored fonts binary; a later line wins for the same path.
# (Merged from the old .gitattributes.)
*.woff2 binary
*.woff binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
# The same for every other binary in the workspace: the landing site's tracked goldens and any picture, sound or movie
# (the game-derived ones are ignored, but a binary must never be normalised if one is ever tracked).
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.ogg binary
*.mp4 binary
*.wav binary
# The committed disc fixtures (RS.R8's size policy, H71): the disc's own bytes -- no eol conversion, no text diff. After
# the `socomlegacy/** text eol=lf` line above, so this one wins; the manifest beside them stays text.
socomlegacy/test-fixtures/RUN/** binary -eol
# RV2-00's recorded replay fixtures (gzip): the same, never normalised -- an LF rewrite would corrupt the gzip stream.
socomlegacy/test-fixtures/replay/** binary -eol
*.s2r binary
